# CODEOWNERS — required reviewers for privileged repository configuration.
#
# Issue #75: the GitHub Actions workflows in this repository run with
# privileged scopes and secrets — `id-token: write` (OIDC) deploying to
# the live GitHub Pages site, plus CODECOV_TOKEN, SEMGREP_APP_TOKEN,
# GITLEAKS_LICENSE and a create-pull-request token. A compromised or
# self-approving account could edit one of these workflows and exfiltrate
# tokens or publish arbitrary content. Requiring an explicit code-owner
# review on every workflow / action change is the canonical
# defence-in-depth control against that supply-chain attack class.
#
# The LAST matching pattern wins, so the workflow and action rules below
# override any broader default added later in the file.

# Workflow and composite-action definitions run with repository secrets —
# require owner review before merge.
/.github/workflows/   @stSoftwareAU/maintainers
/.github/actions/     @stSoftwareAU/maintainers

# The CODEOWNERS policy itself must not be weakened without owner review.
/.github/CODEOWNERS   @stSoftwareAU/maintainers
